// "The Last Steam Knight" (enemy_1533_stmkgt, levels 0 and 1): chapter 11 (11-20, its adverse variant, H11-2 and
// H11-4 adverse). Four native modes: First, Second, HeroBomb_1 and HeroBomb_2.
// - Attack (both forms): the blocked operator, 100% ATK physical at the clip's OnAttack; +1 SP (INCREASE_WHEN_ATTACK).
// - BornWeak (talent): attack speed -50 and movement x(1 - 0.5) (formula MULTIPLIER) until the first Boost.
// - Boost (first form, 45/25 s; level 1 40/40): its effects start with the cast (Boost clip 1 s, no target needed):
//   the debut slow ends; for 15 s attack speed +100, movement x1.3 and control immunity (STUNNED, SILENCED, DISARMED,
//   FROZEN, COLD, LEVITATE, SLEEPING). enemy_stmkgt_boost[buff]: is_hard_level "true" adds 30% damage resistance for
//   the duration; "false" stuns him for `stun` (5 s) when it ends.
// - Zantetsuken (SP 4): locks the blocked operator; Skill_1_Begin charges until `duration` (7 s) less Skill_1_Attack
//   (2.5 s), then `times` (3) hits of 125% ATK physical at Skill_1_Attack's OnAttack (0.7 s). PRTS: 4.5 s charge.
// - HeroBomb (TriggerHeroBomb / _2 hp_ratio 0.5 / 0.3): each time he has lost that ratio of max HP since the mark
//   (spawn, revive end, each HeroBomb's end) and is not casting Zantetsuken, he leaves the ground (invincible,
//   unmovable, OUT_OF_GROUND, control-immune): Skill_2_Begin, an 8 s mark on the 1 / 2 ground operators with the
//   highest max HP, then per selected operator a bombard area on the 3x3 tiles around it (x-4, 9 tiles): every 0.5 s
//   for 5.5 s the unit there with the highest HP ratio takes 50% / 40% ATK Arts 0.2 s later, at most 8 hits; then
//   Skill_2_End. is_hard_level "true" seals the area's buildable tiles (trap_055_tileblock).
// - Revive (reborn, once): the current wave is released; 8 s later he returns at full HP in the second form with 15 s
//   of invincibility, a permanent boost (attack speed +100, movement +0.3 ADDITION, DEF -1500 (level 1 -2000),
//   RES -40, control immunity; reborn.is_hard_level "true" adds 30% damage resistance), and 0.1 s later a HeroBomb.
// Level 1 lists only reborn.def and Boost; like the other sparse higher levels it is read over level zero (talents by
// key, skills by prefab key). Stage skill lists change the named skills in place (11-20 names only the HeroBombs,
// and PRTS lists Boost and Zantetsuken there).
